  https://github.com/actions/checkout/blob/v4/LICENSE
- actions/setup-python v5: MIT
  https://github.com/actions/setup-python/blob/v5/LICENSE
- actions/setup-node v4: MIT
  https://github.com/actions/setup-node/blob/v4/LICENSE
- softprops/action-gh-release v2: MIT
  https://github.com/softprops/action-gh-release/blob/v2/LICENSE
- kewisch/action-web-ext v1: MPL 2.0; see its own additional asset notice
  https://github.com/kewisch/action-web-ext/blob/v1/LICENSE
- mobilefirstllc/cws-publish latest: Apache 2.0
  https://github.com/mobilefirstllc/cws-publish/blob/latest/LICENSE
- Playwright 1.63.0: Apache 2.0
  https://github.com/microsoft/playwright/blob/v1.63.0/LICENSE

Python, Node.js and the browsers are external runtimes governed by their own
licenses. Browser source-code licenses are distinct from the terms of AMO,
Chrome Web Store and other distribution services. Use of those tools and
